%% Extension state machine: proposal → removal, with the kill-switch as a
%% transition from any state. Implemented in runtime/host/registry.py.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Proposed: author opens a proposal<br/>(governance/templates/extension-proposal.md)

  Proposed --> InReview: contract validates<br/>ext validate + ext test pass
  InReview --> Proposed: changes requested
  InReview --> Approved: security + permission review<br/>grant written to approved-grants.yaml

  Approved --> Loaded: registry.load()<br/>parse · grant check · permission diff<br/>capability index · on_load / on_activate
  Approved --> Rejected: permissions not justifiable

  Loaded --> Loaded: patch / minor release<br/>no permission change
  Loaded --> PendingReapproval: upgrade requests NEW permissions<br/>loader refuses, diff surfaced
  PendingReapproval --> Loaded: board re-approves the grant
  PendingReapproval --> Deprecated: expansion rejected

  Loaded --> Deprecated: successor published<br/>or owner steps back
  Deprecated --> Removed: sunset date reached<br/>callers migrated

  Loaded --> Revoked: KILL-SWITCH
  Deprecated --> Revoked: KILL-SWITCH
  PendingReapproval --> Revoked: KILL-SWITCH

  Revoked --> Approved: governance clears the revocation<br/>(incident review, named approver)
  Revoked --> Removed: not coming back

  Removed --> [*]

  note right of Revoked
    host.kill(name, reason, actor):
      · mark revoked in the registry
      · drop capabilities + hook subscriptions
      · broker invalidates every outstanding token
      · audit governance.kill_switch (who, why)
      · reload blocked until cleared
  end note

  note right of Loaded
    Isolation per invocation, by declared runtime:
      local-subprocess · local-inproc (zero-permission only)
      remote-rpc (attested worker) · local-wasm (specified)
  end note
